Aim

To construct a Context Free Grammar (CFG) for a given language, and to design and implement a Pushdown Automaton (PDA) that accepts the language generated by the CFG, using a stack to verify string membership.

 
Theory

Context Free Grammar is a 4-tuple G = (V, T, P, S) where V is a set of non-terminals, T is a set of terminals, P is a set of production rules of the form A→ a (A E V, a E (V U T)*), and S is the start symbol. A Pushdown Automaton extends a finite automaton with an auxiliary stack


Algorithm

1 Define the grammar productions for the target language (e.g., S→ aSb ab for L = {ab" | n≥ 1}).

2 Design the PDA transition rules: push a symbol onto the stack for every 'a' read, and pop a symbol for every 'b' read.

3 Initialize the stack with the bottom marker symbol (e.g., Z0).

4 Read the input string symbol by symbol; for each 'a', push onto the stack; for each 'b', pop from the stack (if stack is empty/only Z0 remains, reject).

5 After the input is fully read, accept if the stack contains only Z0 (empty stack except marker); otherwise
reject


program 


#include <stdio.h>

#include <string.h>

#define MAX 100

char stack[MAX];

int top =-1;

void push(char c) {stack[++top] = c;} 
char pop() { return (top >= 0)? stack[top--]: \'0'; }

int main(){

char str[MAX]; 
int i =0, valid = 1;

printf("PDA for L = { a^n b^n | n>= 1 }\n"); 
printf("Enter input string: ");

scanf("%s", str);

push('Z'); /* stack bottom marker */

/* Phase 1: push 'a' onto stack */

while (str[i]='a') { push('a'); i++; }

if (top == 0) { valid = 0; } /* no 'a' read at all */

/* Phase 2: pop for each 'b' */ while (str[i]= 'b') {

if (top <= 0) { valid = 0; break; } pop();

i++;

}

PDA for L = { a^n b^n | n >= 1 }

Enter input string: aaabbb

String Accepted by PDA (valid a^n b^n)

if (str[i] != \0') valid = 0; if (top != 0) valid = 0;

/* leftover symbols (e.g. another a) */ /* stack must contain only Z0 */

if (valid)

printf("String Accepted by PDA (valid a^n b^n)\n");

else

printf("String Rejected by PDA\n"); 
return 0;

}



